# Alternating Subarray Prefix

Given an array of non-zero integers, find the longest alternating
subarray starting at every index.

An alternating subarray contains adjacent elements with opposite signs.

## Approach

Use Dynamic Programming from right to left.

dp[i] = longest alternating subarray starting at index i.

If A[i] and A[i+1] have opposite signs:

    dp[i] = dp[i+1] + 1

Otherwise:

    dp[i] = 1

## Complexity

Time: O(N)
Space: O(N)

## Example

Input:
[-5, -1, -1, 2, -2, -3]

Output:
[1, 1, 3, 2, 1, 1]
